sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Cl as Client
    participant API as TransferController
    participant TS as TransferService
    participant TX as TransferTransactions<br/>(ONE DB transaction)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant OB as OutboxPublisher
    participant K as Kafka

    Cl->>API: POST /transfers + Idempotency-Key + JWT
    API->>TS: transfer(...)
    TS->>TX: transfer(...)
    TX->>DB: BEGIN
    TX->>DB: INSERT idempotency key ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
    alt key already used
        TX->>DB: read stored result
        TX-->>Cl: 200 original result (Idempotent-Replay: true)
    else new key
        TX->>DB: SELECT both accounts ORDER BY id FOR NO KEY UPDATE
        TX->>TX: fraud rules (limit, daily, velocity)
        TX->>DB: INSERT transaction
        TX->>DB: INSERT ledger entries (-amount, +amount)
        TX->>DB: UPDATE both balances
        TX->>DB: INSERT outbox event
        TX->>DB: UPDATE idempotency key with transaction id
        TX->>DB: COMMIT (trigger checks ledger sums to 0)
        TX-->>Cl: 201 Created
    end
    loop every 500 ms
        OB->>DB: claim unpublished rows (SKIP LOCKED)
        OB->>K: send TRANSFER_COMPLETED
        OB->>DB: mark published
    end
    K->>K: NotificationConsumer creates DEBIT / CREDIT notifications
    Note over TS: If a fraud rule blocked it, the transaction has<br/>rolled back, and only then is the fraud alert saved.
